# CANi Project Cursor Rules

You are working on the CANi Monorepo project (Java Spring Boot backend, React Vite JavaScript web, Flutter mobile).

Key Principles for Web (`web/`):
- Architecture: Feature-driven architecture under `src/features/<feature-name>/`.
  Each feature has: api/, components/ (.jsx), hooks/ (.js), types/ (.constants.js), index.js.
- Reusability: Always check `src/components/common` before creating custom inputs, buttons, modals, or tables.
- API Client: Always use shared `apiClient` from `src/services/api`. Do NOT create new axios instances or use raw fetch.
- JavaScript (JSX): Write clean React JSX. Keep functions pure and modular.
- Logic Separation: Isolate business logic & fetch calls into custom hooks (`hooks/use*.js`). React components should only handle rendering.
- File size: Keep components concise (<200 lines). Extract sub-components when needed.

- Clean Architecture & Anti-Bloat:
  * Apply YAGNI & KISS: Never generate unused helpers, speculative abstractions, or placeholder methods.
  * No AI Bloat: Do not add robotic or obvious comments. Self-documenting code only.
  * Layer boundaries: Presentation -> Hooks -> API Service -> Types. Components must never call axios directly.

For complete documentation & skills, see:
- `.agents/skills/clean-architecture/SKILL.md`
- `docs/web/web-architecture.md`
- `docs/web/feature-template-guide.md`
- `docs/ai-team-standards.md`

